-
-export const aLandingSettlesItsLockfileAfterTheCommitSoAFailedInstallLeavesMainBroken = {
-  id: "01a076d5-bf60-75fd-be1f-99889db09e80",
-  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
-  slug: "a-landing-settles-its-lockfile-after-the-commit-so-a-failed-install-leaves-main-broken",
-  domainSlug: "page-type/change",
-
-  claim:
-    "A landing carrying a `package.json` settles the lockfile by installing once that landing has given up the hold, so the commit is on main before the install is tried. An install that fails there leaves the commit on main with a lockfile naming what the manifests named before. Nothing retries it and nothing takes the landing back; the call exits non-zero after the commit is already unreachable to undo. A checkout whose `node_modules` is warm reads as healthy, because the links reach the packages under both names, so the breakage is visible only where nothing is installed yet: a deploy's staging clone, or a pod that clones at start.",
-  evidence:
-    'Measured 2026-09-06, expanding the rename of `@akasha/code-system` to `@akasha/code`.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. `akasha patch apply` exited 3 saying `error: @akasha/code-system@workspace:@akasha/code@* failed to resolve`, and then that the lockfile is made without an install, so what the workspace reaches its packages through still points at the folders the manifests named before, and that a landing carrying a `package.json` installs the checkout to move it, once that landing has given up the hold. Both commits landed regardless: ab4f748b1a and e493f7f6c2.\n\nWHAT LANDED. `git show --stat ab4f748b1a` names 14 files, every one of them a `package.json`, and no lockfile among them. `bun.lock` still carries `"name": "@akasha/code-system"` at line 518 and `"@akasha/code-system": "workspace:*"` at 465 and at nine more, while `code-system/package.json` now says `"name": "@akasha/code"`.\n\nWHERE IT BIT. Amy measured `akasha deploy alanwalton --ref 6941e3a875` failing on the Mac at `bun install` with `Workspace dependency "@akasha/code-system" not found. Searched in "./@akasha/code@*"`. The workstation was fine throughout, its `node_modules` holding `@akasha/code` and `@akasha/code-system` as two links onto one folder.\n\nWHAT IS NOT THE FAULT. The alias form is good. Amy built the isolated case — a root manifest naming `"@probe/old-name": "workspace:@probe/new-name@*"` beside an inner package called `@probe/new-name` — and bun 1.3.14 installs it clean. I had claimed the opposite from a control that deleted the alias line and watched the install go green; that does not discriminate, since deleting the line also takes away the only thing that has to resolve the stale name, and it passes under either reading.\n\nHOW LONG THE WINDOW HAS BEEN OPEN. The lockfile settles at contract rather than at expand: the previous rename\'s lockfile commit is aec38b62ff, `take the alias for @akasha/pages-system-service away`. So every package rename has left this window open between expand and contract, and the two before this one closed only because nobody installed cold while they were open.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. Whether anything anywhere retries the settling install was not measured, and neither was whether a landing that carries a `package.json` for any other reason reaches the same state.',
-} as const satisfies Finding
